EXPERIMENT 48 – REGRESSION TEST SUITE USING TAGS AND TEST SUITES IN JUNIT
AIM
To write JUnit test cases to create a regression test suite using tags and test suites in JUnit.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add junit-jupiter and junit-platform-suite dependencies.
2. Create the CartService class with addItem(), removeItem(), total() and totalWithDiscount() methods.
3. Create CartTest and mark tests using @Tag("smoke") and @Tag("regression").
4. Create RegressionSuiteTest using @Suite, @SelectClasses and @IncludeTags("regression").
5. Run using mvn test -Dtest=RegressionSuiteTest.
6. Verify that only four regression tests are executed.
CODE
1. CartService.java
import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class CartService {
    private final Map<String, Double> items =
        new LinkedHashMap<>();

    public void addItem(String name, double price) {
        items.put(name, price);
    }

    public boolean removeItem(String name) {
        return items.remove(name) != null;
    }

    public int size() {
        return items.size();
    }

    public double total() {
        return items.values().stream()
            .mapToDouble(Double::doubleValue).sum();
    }

    public double totalWithDiscount(double percent) {
        return total() * (100 - percent) / 100;
    }
}


2. CartTest.java
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Tag;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class CartTest {

    @Test
    @Tag("smoke")
    @Tag("regression")
    void addItemIncreasesSize() {
        CartService cart = new CartService();
        cart.addItem("Pen", 10);
        assertEquals(1, cart.size());
    }

    @Test
    @Tag("regression")
    void removeItemWorks() {
        CartService cart = new CartService();
        cart.addItem("Pen", 10);
        assertTrue(cart.removeItem("Pen"));
        assertEquals(0, cart.size());
    }

    @Test
    @Tag("regression")
    void totalOfTwoItems() {
        CartService cart = new CartService();
        cart.addItem("Pen", 100);
        cart.addItem("Book", 250);
        assertEquals(350, cart.total(), 0.001);
    }

    @Test
    @Tag("smoke")
    void emptyCartTotalIsZero() {
        assertEquals(0,
            new CartService().total(), 0.001);
    }

    @Test
    @Tag("regression")
    void discountIsApplied() {
        CartService cart = new CartService();
        cart.addItem("Pen", 100);
        cart.addItem("Book", 250);
        assertEquals(315,
            cart.totalWithDiscount(10), 0.001);
    }
}


3. RegressionSuiteTest.java
import org.junit.platform.suite.api.IncludeTags;
import org.junit.platform.suite.api.SelectClasses;
import org.junit.platform.suite.api.Suite;

@Suite
@SelectClasses(CartTest.class)
@IncludeTags("regression")
public class RegressionSuiteTest {
}


INPUT
Test Case	Input	Expected Output
Add item	Pen, 10	Size = 1
Remove item	Pen	Size = 0
Total of two items	100 + 250	350
Empty cart	No items	0
Apply discount	10% on 350	315

OUTPUT
$ mvn test -Dtest=RegressionSuiteTest

Running RegressionSuiteTest

Tests run: 4
Failures: 0
Errors: 0
Skipped: 0

BUILD SUCCESS


RESULT
Thus, JUnit test cases were executed successfully to create a regression test suite using tags and test suites, and the output was verified.
